Goldens for chat_template_qwen4_exp. Rendered from the published template
https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/raw/main/chat_template.jinja
(sha256 af16f654968d47d09a6c604e00370b12dbc21f76456f59c9e98b82e84d9f6375) with
jinja2 3.0.3, a custom Environment registering `raise_exception` and an extension that
renders {% generation %}...{% endgeneration %} transparently. Inputs per file name:
messages S=system U=user A=assistant(reasoning_content), add_generation_prompt=True unless noted.
inline_think_preserve / inline_think_drop_old: U "2+2?", A content "<think>\nAdd the numbers.\n</think>\n\n4"
with NO reasoning_content, U "And 3+3?"; preserve_thinking true / false. The published template
has no `'</think>' in content` split (its only `</think>` literals are jinja lines 119 and 170);
line 103 trims content and lines 110-122 wrap it in an empty reasoning block or emit it verbatim.

#7336 (tools and vision branches). `chat_template.jinja` is the published file, verbatim
(same sha256; a test asserts it). tools_*.txt and vision_*.txt were NOT rendered with jinja2
(no Python in this repo): tests_qwen4_exp.rs renders chat_template.jinja with minijinja and
asserts each golden equals that render AND the Rust renderer. The same minijinja setup
replays the nine jinja2 goldens above byte for byte, which is the evidence that it reads the
template as jinja2 does. Supplied to minijinja by the test: `raise_exception`,
`str.startswith/endswith`, `{% generation %}` removed (transparent block), and `tojson` =
Python `json.dumps(x, ensure_ascii=False)` as `transformers` registers it (", " and ": "
separators). Not measured: a jinja2 / transformers render of the tools_* inputs. Object keys
are in sorted order in these goldens. The tool fixtures in tests_qwen4_exp.rs are written in
sorted key order too, so the goldens hold whether serde_json's `preserve_order` is off
(aprender-core built alone) or on (workspace build); the Rust renderer emits keys in the
order the `serde_json::Value` holds them and does not sort.
Regenerate: QWEN4EXP_BLESS_DIR=<dir> cargo test -p aprender-core --lib chat_template_qwen4_exp
Jinja lines: tools system block 57-75; tool calls 123-147; tool responses 151-162; vision
content parts 3-41 (inputs: tools_system_user S U + tools [get_weather, now];
tools_no_system_medium U + [get_weather], reasoning_effort medium; tools_call_and_response
S U A(tool_call get_weather{city,days}) T; tools_two_calls_drop_old U A(content + 2 calls)
T T A U, preserve_thinking false; vision_image_text U[image, text]; vision_ids_two_turns
S U[image, video, text] A U[text, image, video], add_vision_id true).
